{"title":"1973 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 15th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> 1973 in USSR. \n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d086777311e5d4830649e795f6946cacfa47097f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_1}, \\overrightarrow{OP_2}, \\ldots, \\overrightarrow{OP_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"150\" height=\"25\" /> are unit vectors such that points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a6ed700c0ce50f74d1a209905b3da01243314ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> all lie in a plane containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and on one side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d3e2b0a8614100059053cda6b99ce99ee2802d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\vert \\overrightarrow{OP_1} + \\overrightarrow{OP_2} + \\ldots + \\overrightarrow{OP_n} \\right\\vert \\geq 1\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"34\" />\nHere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/f/d3fb4da3e6f4e9038bde34b52c7f6fcf980d9155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\vert \\overrightarrow{OM} \\right\\vert$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"34\" /> denotes the length of vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/7778b0df233f81dfd150a7001810d10f675d74d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OM}$\" width=\"33\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine whether or not there exists a finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> of points in space not lying in the same plane such that, for any two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, one can select two other points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> so that lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are parallel and not coincident.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be real numbers for which the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bcfbfe57d245060e637e48e76d304223e1474cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^4 + ax^3 + bx^2 + ax + 1 = 0\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"16\" />\nhas at least one real solution. For all such pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, find the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/d/d7d3200f508f2bf0ee872dcc13ec904170623dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A soldier needs to check on the presence of mines in a region having the shape of an equilateral triangle. The radius of action of his detector is equal to half the altitude of the triangle. The soldier leaves from one vertex of the\ntriangle. What path should he follow in order to travel the least possible distance and still accomplish his mission?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a set of non-constant functions of the real variable <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> of the form\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c91970a59b47c8979480c342223fb79fce997af3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) = ax + b, a \\text{ and } b \\text{ are real numbers,}\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"18\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has the following properties:\n</p><p>(a) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/83637413b74ace90ba737c190bc4613d99fcede3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g \\circ f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> is in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cdf4b8f88415a15fd422f9b4c16636d7a6e2f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(g \\circ f)(x) = g[f(x)]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>(b) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then its inverse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/74153d34ed1e2096b5c034cb85eff5a695b887c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> is in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; here the inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d36e0d4659d4f5dc0d8a325d32f94c14f848f7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = ax + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689a1ad2facd275ef7f12d70fefc60ffe3e5dfb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{-1}(x) = (x - b) / a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>(c) For every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, there exists a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67ada7f9d2a055fd6b1a64ebe5e53a566410af37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/1670c83bfdeec592d8bacc85d0ed38462eac2d42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_f) = x_f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Prove that there exists a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b921999fc591ae97fd07de5c6d3102498afb2ac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k) = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a25c2f9720d16d7ab307b6766d3539fad0a05b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive numbers, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a given real number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9ed2f9639294e1be1d879cf25c787ba608272b4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; q &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e712ff3c1efcd54de88fdbe99450fed2d84ad55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> for which\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/179606b6593cfc807c3f77be840f367898d9f4f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k &lt; b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb14695a8722d9fa057b67bd4d83b02c09038f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, 2, \\ldots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35a1a13926d50ef5f6f86b9d17ef35548e123f0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q &lt; \\tfrac{b_{k+1}}{b_k} &lt; \\tfrac {1}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"97\" height=\"25\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/879ac8e3b91dda6eebe97005c7a19578f0dc398d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, 2, \\ldots, n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a55619d76b8a366a6d5d7d3006a6019a06c709e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 + b_2 + \\cdots + b_n &lt; \\tfrac{1 + q}{1 - q} (a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"340\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO\" title=\"1973 IMO\">1973 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1973\">IMO 1973 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO\" title=\"1973 IMO\">1973 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_IMO\" title=\"1972 IMO\">1972 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_IMO\" title=\"1974 IMO\">1974 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018042201\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 318/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 837/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10690/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.896      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.896      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8942:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018042201 and revision id 143876. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}